tree-sitter-angular-html adapts material from one MIT-licensed project.

The external scanner (src/scanner.c) derives from tree-sitter-html's scanner
(https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-html), copyright (c) 2014 Max
Brunsfeld, licensed under the MIT License. The adaptation keeps its
open-element stack, implicit end tag rules, raw text and comment scanning,
and adds Angular-aware text, quoted attribute text that stops at `{{`, and
block markers on the element stack for `@if`/`@for`/`@switch`/`@defer`
braces. Tag names are stored as strings instead of an enum of known tags.

The HTML node names (element, start_tag, attribute, quoted_attribute_value,
...) follow tree-sitter-html's so existing queries carry over. The grammar
rules themselves are written from scratch.
